- The integer array parameter `nums` may contain duplicate elements.
- The integer array result contains lists of integers, each list representing a triplet `[nums[i], nums[j], nums[k]]` where `i != j`, `i != k`, and `j != k`.
- The integer array result does not contain duplicate triplets.
- The sum of elements in each triplet in the integer array result is equal to 0.
- The length of each list in the integer array result is equal to 3.
- The integer array result may be empty if no triplets satisfy the conditions.